@startuml
' C4-style component view without a remote include.
' Parent document: README.md

title DASHI periodic Navier–Stokes Clay contract

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 160
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Mathematical reviewer" as Reviewer

package "Official requirement boundary" {
  component "Fefferman periodic alternative B\nExact preconditions and postconditions" as ClayTarget <<Requirement>>
}

package "Finite analytic system" {
  component "Finite Galerkin PDE\nfiltered vorticity and enstrophy" as Galerkin <<Component>>
  component "Directional defect evolution\npair-input-frequency damping" as Defect <<Component>>
  component "Five-source physical taxation" as Tax <<Open producer>>
  component "Strict viscosity certificate" as Margin <<Open producer>>
}

package "Limit and continuation system" {
  component "Critical Grönwall reducer" as Gronwall <<Checked reducer>>
  component "Nested shell/Galerkin limits" as Limits <<Reducer plus open analysis>>
  component "Critical restart" as Restart <<Reducer plus open analysis>>
  component "Smooth velocity and pressure recovery" as Recovery <<Open producer>>
}

package "Submission adaptation system" {
  component "Legacy global physical witness" as Legacy <<Existing interface>>
  component "Legacy-to-Fefferman adapter" as Adapter <<Checked reducer>>
  component "Mean-zero centering and Galilean restoration" as Galilean <<Reducer plus open analysis>>
  component "Literal Fefferman witness" as Literal <<Target witness>>
}

package "Assurance system" {
  component "Round 23 cumulative Agda root" as AgdaRoot <<Verification>>
  component "Static no-hole and provenance checker" as Checker <<Verification>>
  component "Change, risk and traceability record" as Governance <<Governance>>
}

Galerkin --> Defect : actual Fourier cells
Defect --> Tax : five named source terms
Tax --> Margin : explicit viscosity allocations
Margin --> Gronwall : total coefficient < 1
Gronwall --> Limits : uniform critical estimate
Limits --> Restart : bounded physical critical norm
Restart --> Recovery : infinite maximal time
Recovery --> Legacy : global smooth solution data
Legacy --> Adapter : stronger witness
Adapter --> Galilean : centered literal witness
Galilean --> Literal : arbitrary periodic datum
Literal --> ClayTarget : inhabits exact theorem type

AgdaRoot ..> Galerkin : imports
AgdaRoot ..> Defect : imports
AgdaRoot ..> Gronwall : imports
AgdaRoot ..> Limits : imports
AgdaRoot ..> Restart : imports
AgdaRoot ..> Adapter : imports
AgdaRoot ..> Galilean : imports
Checker ..> AgdaRoot : executes pinned Agda check
Governance ..> Checker : quality and change gates
Reviewer --> Governance : reviews evidence
Reviewer --> ClayTarget : checks source fidelity

note right of Tax
Open: uniform physical bounds in q, Q and N.
No generic remainder is permitted.
end note

note right of Galilean
Mean zero is a reduction device,
not a Clay precondition.
end note

note bottom of ClayTarget
No unconditional theorem is promoted
until every open producer is inhabited
and the cumulative kernel check passes.
end note

@enduml
